Amendment 934
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CHAPTER 3, SECTIONS 42 AND 44 OF THE
REVISED ORDINANCES OF 2008 TO RELATIVE TO ADDING JUNETEENTH 
AS A PAID HOLIDAY
Be it ordained by the City Council of the City of Worcester as follows:
Section 1. Chapter 3 of the Revised Ordinances of 2008 be and is hereby amended by
deleting section 42 in its entirety and inserting a new section 42 as follows:
§ 42. Holiday Leave
(a) Subject to the rules and regulations promulgated by the city manager, full-time civilian 
employees of the city shall be entitled to twelve paid holidays enumerated below in
addition to any regular days off to which they may be entitled:
(1) First day ofJanuary or the day preceding when said day occurs on a Saturday, or the 
day following when said day occurs on a Sunday;
(2) Third Monday in January;
(3) Third Monday in February;
(4) Third Monday in April;
(5)Last Monday in May;
(6) Fourth day of July or the day preceding when said day occurs on a Saturday, or the 
day following when said day occurs on a Sunday;
(7) First Monday in September;
(8) Second Monday in October;
(9) Eleventh day of November or the day proceeding when said day occurs on a
Saturday, or the day following when said day occurs on a Sunday;
(10) A day in November proclaimed as Thanksgiving Day;
(11) Christmas Day or the day preceding when said day occurs on a Saturday, or the
day following when said day occurs on a Sunday;
(12) Nineteenth day ofJune or the day preceding when said day occurs on a Saturday,
or the day following when said day occurs on a Sunday;
